==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*hwō}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|hū}}, {{cog|osx|hū}} ({{cog|nl|hoe}}), {{cog|goh|wuo}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|hū}}

===Adverb===
{{ang-adv|hū}}

# [[how]], in all senses, including:
## to [[what]] [[degree]]
##: {{ux|ang|'''Hū''' eald is þīn dohtor?|'''How''' old is your daughter?}}
##: {{ux|ang|'''Hū''' miċel gold hæfst þū on þē?|'''How''' much gold do you have on you?}}
## in [[what]] [[manner]]
##: {{ux|ang|'''Hū''' sæġþ man þæt on Englisċ?|'''How''' do you say that in English?}}
##: {{ux|ang|'''Hū''' færest þū?|'''How''' are you? (Literally: "'''How''' are you faring?")}}
## in [[what]] [[state]]
##: {{ux|ang|'''Hū''' wæs þīn dæġ?|'''How''' was your day?}}
##: {{ux|ang|Þū canst Ælfrēd cyning? '''Hū''' is hē?|You know King Alfred? '''What''' is he '''like'''?}}
# {{n-g|used in exclamations}}
#* '''c. 995''', [[w:Ælfric of Eynsham|Ælfric]], [https://archive.org/stream/grammatik00aelfuoft#page/n249 ''Extracts on Grammar in English'']
#*: {{quote|ang|''Ēalā '''hū''' gōd mann!''|Oh, '''what''' a good person!}}
# {{n-g|used to introduce negative rhetorical questions}}
#* '''late 9th century''', [[w:Alfred the Great|King Alfred's]] [https://books.google.com/books?id=8sy8OOmW-ZAC&pg=PA8 translation] of [[w:Boethius|Boethius']] ''{{w|The Consolation of Philosophy}}''
#*: {{quote|ang|'''''Hū''', ne eart þū sē mann þe on mīnre scōle wǣre āfēded and ġelǣred?''|Aren't you the person who was raised and taught in my school?}}

====Descendants====
* {{desctree|enm|how}}

===Conjunction===
{{ang-con|head=hū}}

# [[how]], in all senses:
## in [[what]] [[manner]]
##: {{ux|ang|Iċ leornode '''hū''' man wæġn ġebētt.|I learned '''how''' to repair a wagon.}}
##: {{ux|ang|Hīe āscodon '''hū''' hīe helpan meahten.|They asked '''how''' they could help.}}
## [[that]], the fact that ''(introducing direct statements)''
##: {{ux|ang|Iċ him sæġde '''hū''' iċ wǣre æt hām ealne dæġ and ne ġehīerde nāwiht.|I told them '''how''' I'd been at home all day and hadn't heard a thing.}}
##: {{ux|ang|Þæt is tō wundriġenne '''hū''' hīe þā bryċġe swā hrædlīċe ġefyldon.|It's amazing '''how''' they completed the bridge so quickly.}}

====Descendants====
